---
/* oberrieden.pub/review -> the pub's Google listing.

   Exists so printed material can carry a short, readable address instead of a
   seventy-character Google URL. Two further reasons it is worth a page:

   - A short URL makes a far less dense QR code, which scans from further away
     across a pub.
   - If the Google link ever changes, this file changes and every printed
     banner keeps working. Nothing has to be reprinted.

   Deliberately not built on Base.astro: no fonts, no stylesheet, no images.
   Nobody should ever see this page for more than an instant, so it carries the
   redirect, a visible link for anyone whose browser blocks it, and nothing
   else. */
import { pub } from "../../data/pub";

const target = pub.googleReview;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`0; url=${target}`} />
    <title>Big Ben Pub — review us on Google</title>
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        background: #531c23;
        color: #f0e8dc;
        font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, Arial, sans-serif;
        text-align: center;
        padding: 24px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      a { color: #ddba7a }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>
      Taking you to Google &hellip;<br />
      <a href={target}>Big Ben Pub on Google</a>
    </p>
    <script is:inline define:vars={{ target }}>
      location.replace(target);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
